# Docker build-context hygiene.
#
# Without this file the app-level `COPY apps/<app> ./apps/<app>` steps copy the
# host's `node_modules` (pnpm junctions/symlinks created on the developer's
# machine) over the symlinks that `pnpm install` just created inside the image.
# Those host links point outside the image, so `tsc`/`vite` fail with
# "Cannot find module '/app/apps/<app>/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc'".
# It also keeps the context small (the pnpm virtual store is hundreds of MB).

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.pnpm-store
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local/env-only files — containers receive configuration through the compose
# environment, never from a baked-in .env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Repository plumbing not needed to build any image.
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
e2e
